{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.TauMAsymptoticRepTheory","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.TauMAsymptoticRepTheory","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.tau_M_asymptotic_rep_theory","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.tau_M_asymptotic_rep_theory","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L98-L120","doc":"**Asymptotic-expansion synthesis theorem.** The Kashiwara crystal\nprovides the canonical c_k generator with two concrete pinned\nvalues: `c_0 = 0` and `c_1 = b_λ`. The other three anchors\n(Jucys-Murphy, Macdonald, Habiro) provide their own coefficient\nfunctions; the synthesis at the class level extracts the Kashiwara\n`c_k` as the canonical export.\n\nThe agreement of the four anchors at higher `k` is per-irrep\ncombinatorial content that lives outside the class axiomatisation;\nhere we only export the Kashiwara generator + its low-order pinning. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory","label":"prop:tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidue.residue_sum_at_root_of_unity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidue.residue_sum_at_root_of_unity","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L85-L85","doc":"Finite residue sum at q = ζ_N. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidue.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidue.mk","kind":"ctor","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroResidue","kind":"class","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L82-L85","doc":"**Habiro residue summation** for `V_λ` at a primitive N-th root of unity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MacdonaldZonal.inner_product_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MacdonaldZonal.inner_product_coeff","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L78-L78","doc":"⟨P_λ(·; q, q²), P_λ(·; q, q²)⟩ — k-th coefficient of (q,t)-inner-product expansion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MacdonaldZonal.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MacdonaldZonal.mk","kind":"ctor","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MacdonaldZonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MacdonaldZonal","kind":"class","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L75-L78","doc":"**Macdonald (q, t) pairing data** at `t = q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphySpectrum.p_1_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphySpectrum.p_1_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L71-L71","doc":"Concrete pinning: `p_1 = 0` on V_(2,1) (antisymmetric eigenvalues\n±h sum to zero) — the diagonal JM trace vanishes at first order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphySpectrum.power_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphySpectrum.power_sum","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Power-sum symmetric function p_k(J_2, ..., J_n) on V_λ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphySpectrum.content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphySpectrum.content","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L66-L66","doc":"q-content of cell containing label k in SYT T. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphySpectrum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphySpectrum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphySpectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphySpectrum","kind":"class","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L63-L71","doc":"**Jucys-Murphy spectral data** for `V_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KashiwaraCrystal.c_1_eq_b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KashiwaraCrystal.c_1_eq_b","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KashiwaraCrystal.c_0_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KashiwaraCrystal.c_0_zero","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Concrete pinning: `c_0 = 0` (baseline form) and `c_1 = b_lambda`\n(Kashiwara `f̃_1` matrix element). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KashiwaraCrystal.c_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KashiwaraCrystal.c_k","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Crystal-graph matrix-element polynomial at level k. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KashiwaraCrystal.b_lambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KashiwaraCrystal.b_lambda","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Off-diagonal coupling (single scalar at H_3; matrix at higher n). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KashiwaraCrystal.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KashiwaraCrystal.mk","kind":"ctor","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KashiwaraCrystal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KashiwaraCrystal","kind":"class","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L45-L56","doc":"**Kashiwara crystal-graph axiomatisation** for `V_λ`. Encodes\nthe Hoefsmit off-diagonal coupling `b_λ` and the crystal-energy\ncoefficients `c_k(b_λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/tau-M-asymptotic-rep-theory.lean#L35-L36","doc":"Quantum Planck constant `ℏ_q = (q - 1) / q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}